      {
        "id": "lem-gaussian-convolution-kl-and-log-square-second-order-bound",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Gaussian convolution has second-order KL and log-square error",
        "deps": [
          "lem-normal-location-scale-density",
          "cor-cauchy-schwarz-inequality-for-l-two",
          "thm-tonelli-theorem-for-sigma-finite-product-spaces",
          "def-kullback-leibler-divergence",
          "def-axiom-of-choice"
        ],
        "statement": "Assume AC. Let $p\\in C^2(\\mathbb R)$ be a nonnegative compactly supported probability density and suppose\n$$ J:=\\int_{\\{p>0\\}}\\frac{(p''(x))^2}{p(x)}\\,dx<\\infty. $$\nFor $\\sigma>0$, set $q_\\sigma=p*\\phi_\\sigma$, where $\\phi_\\sigma$ is the centered normal density with standard deviation $\\sigma$. Then\n$$ \\int\\frac{(p-q_\\sigma)^2}{q_\\sigma}\\,dx\\le\\frac49\\sigma^4J,\\qquad \\mathrm{KL}(p\\Vert q_\\sigma)\\le\\frac49\\sigma^4J,\\qquad \\int p\\left[\\log\\frac p{q_\\sigma}\\right]^2dx\\le\\frac49\\sigma^4J. $$\nThe logarithmic integrands are zero where $p=0$. No unimodality or uniform bound on $p/q_\\sigma$ is assumed.\n\n",
        "dependency_level": 1
      },
