      {
        "id": "lem-dirichlet-normal-mixture-interval-mass-local-prior-mass",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Interval masses give a log-free local KL neighborhood for the mixture prior",
        "deps": [
          "lem-gaussian-convolution-kl-and-log-square-second-order-bound",
          "lem-dirichlet-normal-mixture-finite-support-approximation",
          "lem-dirichlet-process-simplex-small-ball",
          "lem-dirichlet-normal-mixture-density-well-defined",
          "lem-normal-location-scale-density",
          "def-axiom-of-choice"
        ],
        "statement": "Assume AC. Let $p_0\\in C^2(\\mathbb R)$ be a probability density with compact support $K$, a finite union of intervals. Suppose $J=\\int_{\\{p_0>0\\}}(p_0'')^2/p_0<\\infty$ and there are $a,c>0$ such that $P_0(I)\\ge c\\lambda(I)^a$ for every interval $I\\subseteq K$. Let $F\\sim DP(\\alpha)$, where $\\alpha$ is a finite nonzero measure with continuous strictly positive density on a neighborhood of $K$, and independently let $S\\sim G$ for any probability measure $G$ on $(0,\\infty)$. Suppose $n^{-a_1}\\lesssim\\sigma_n\\lesssim n^{-a_2}$ for $0<a_2<a_1<1$, and put $\\sigma=\\sigma_nS$. Then for constants $C_1,C_2>0$ and all sufficiently large $n$,\n$$ \\Pi_n\\left\\{\\mathrm{KL}(P_0\\Vert P_{F,\\sigma})\\le C_1\\sigma_n^4,\\quad P_0\\left[\\log\\frac{p_0}{p_{F,\\sigma}}\\right]^2\\le C_1\\sigma_n^4\\right\\}\\ge\\exp\\{-C_2\\sigma_n^{-1}(\\log n)^2\\}. $$\nConsequently, for $d_n=\\max\\{(n\\sigma_n)^{-1/2}\\log n,\\sigma_n^2\\}$, the same two local quantities are at most $C_1d_n^2$ on a set of prior mass at least $e^{-C_3nd_n^2}$. Logarithmic integrands vanish where $p_0=0$.\n\n",
        "dependency_level": 6
      },
      {
